1
00:00:19,019 --> 00:00:22,422
I wish that Mr. Akira
never wins mah-jong again.

2
00:00:22,655 --> 00:00:24,991
Oh my, what a petty wish.

3
00:00:25,058 --> 00:00:27,060
You already won twice this week!

4
00:00:27,327 --> 00:00:29,996
I wish that the price
of melons to go down.

5
00:00:30,063 --> 00:00:31,631
- Whose is petty?
- Yours, of course.

6
00:00:31,698 --> 00:00:34,234
Don't quarrel in front of God.

7
00:00:35,769 --> 00:00:38,972
I wish my daughter Mai
becomes a prima donna.

8
00:00:41,941 --> 00:00:46,413
God, please grant this
single mother's wish.

9
00:00:46,546 --> 00:00:49,082
We'll take back our petty wishes.

10
00:00:49,215 --> 00:00:53,019
Mai is currently studying abroad
at a ballet school in England.

11
00:00:53,086 --> 00:00:55,522
She is a very talented and good girl.

12
00:00:55,588 --> 00:00:57,490
Please make Mai a prima donna.

13
00:00:58,391 --> 00:00:59,492
Thank you.

14
00:01:00,627 --> 00:01:02,695
- let's go buy something!
- Buy with your money.

15
00:01:02,762 --> 00:01:03,696
But wait...

16
00:01:07,934 --> 00:01:09,202
- Sorry.
- Okay, let's go.

17
00:01:09,335 --> 00:01:11,571
- Let's buy some takoyaki.
- Buy it with your money.

18
00:01:12,572 --> 00:01:15,208
Why are there so many
pregnant women here?

19
00:01:15,642 --> 00:01:18,545
The god of this shrine helps
women have a safe delivery.

20
00:01:18,611 --> 00:01:22,182
I came here with my ex-husband
when I was pregnant with Mai.

21
00:01:24,250 --> 00:01:26,553
- Hey! Hey!
- Huh? What is it?

22
00:01:28,354 --> 00:01:29,389
Move. Hurry.

23
00:01:29,456 --> 00:01:30,824
- Look over there.
- Where?

24
00:01:35,128 --> 00:01:35,995
Here you go.

25
00:01:39,599 --> 00:01:40,967
Isn't he the Chief Surgeon...

26
00:01:41,234 --> 00:01:42,502
and his wife?

27
00:01:42,836 --> 00:01:45,538
She's too young to be his wife.

28
00:01:46,072 --> 00:01:48,741
I wish the baby'll be safely born

29
00:01:49,309 --> 00:01:50,443
as beautiful as you.

30
00:01:51,411 --> 00:01:52,979
You're so kind.

31
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:54,714
Let's go.

32
00:01:55,281 --> 00:02:01,354
The lustful Chief Surgeon, Saionji,
finally made his lover pregnant.

33
00:02:01,888 --> 00:02:03,456
Adultery again?

34
00:02:04,257 --> 00:02:05,658
What a scumbag.

35
00:02:06,726 --> 00:02:09,929
This is the story of
a lone wolf woman doctor.

36
00:02:11,865 --> 00:02:13,032
<i>In 2016,</i>

37
00:02:13,233 --> 00:02:16,202
<i>the once sacrosanct university</i>
<i>medical system was in crisis.</i>

38
00:02:16,769 --> 00:02:18,738
<i>The system on which lives depend</i>

39
00:02:19,239 --> 00:02:21,074
<i>had strayed away from what it should be.</i>

40
00:02:21,908 --> 00:02:22,842
We've been waiting for you.

41
00:02:23,643 --> 00:02:25,345
<i>Famous university hospitals use...</i>

42
00:02:25,879 --> 00:02:28,014
<i>their brand power</i>
<i>to push into the world.</i>

43
00:02:28,281 --> 00:02:30,850
<i>On the other hand,</i>
<i>highly skilled surgeons...</i>

44
00:02:31,251 --> 00:02:34,387
<i>in pursuit of a higher salary...</i>
<i>were relocating to foreign countries.</i>

45
00:02:34,954 --> 00:02:37,824
<i>The world of medicine has entered...</i>

46
00:02:37,891 --> 00:02:41,127
<i>into the global world</i>
<i>of survival of the fittest.</i>

47
00:02:41,194 --> 00:02:42,462
- Good morning.
- Hey,

48
00:02:42,629 --> 00:02:44,697
I wonder what kind of
person his lover can be.

49
00:02:44,764 --> 00:02:45,598
Well.

50
00:02:45,732 --> 00:02:48,768
Hey, who is she?

51
00:02:49,602 --> 00:02:52,405
She's a very famous celebrity
who got married in Shanghai.

52
00:02:52,605 --> 00:02:55,341
Her husband is famous.
Runs a conglomerate in China...

53
00:02:55,408 --> 00:02:57,210
and buys out all real estates in Japan.

54
00:02:57,777 --> 00:02:59,879
That means it's double infidelities.

55
00:03:00,914 --> 00:03:01,948
That's so nasty.

56
00:03:02,549 --> 00:03:03,416
What's nasty?

57
00:03:03,616 --> 00:03:05,451
Who's having an affair?

58
00:03:05,518 --> 00:03:07,453
Your own chief.

59
00:03:08,788 --> 00:03:10,757
- No way!
- What does she mean?

60
00:03:18,164 --> 00:03:19,399
I can't take it anymore!

61
00:03:22,669 --> 00:03:25,471
Please help! The baby is coming out.

62
00:03:26,239 --> 00:03:27,273
Are you okay?

63
00:03:27,707 --> 00:03:30,577
- The baby is about to come out.
- Do you have a reservation?

64
00:03:30,643 --> 00:03:33,513
What? It's an emergency!

65
00:03:33,580 --> 00:03:34,547
I'm terribly sorry...

66
00:03:34,747 --> 00:03:36,783
but our maternity ward is full.

67
00:03:38,851 --> 00:03:42,956
<i>In the midst of it,</i>
<i>a new breed of doctor has emerged.</i>

68
00:03:43,590 --> 00:03:46,659
<i>Freelance doctors,</i>
<i>in other words, lone wolf doctors.</i>

69
00:03:47,427 --> 00:03:49,362
She's crowning.
Let's get her to a delivery room.

70
00:03:49,429 --> 00:03:50,496
Bring a stretcher!

71
00:03:50,563 --> 00:03:51,431
No.

72
00:03:51,831 --> 00:03:54,200
The baby is coming out.
Should she give a birth here?

73
00:03:54,267 --> 00:03:56,536
Such unexpected delivery
accompanies high risk.

74
00:03:56,603 --> 00:03:57,604
Bring a stretcher!

75
00:03:58,471 --> 00:03:59,472
Dr. Daimon!

76
00:03:59,539 --> 00:04:00,673
Thank you.

77
00:04:00,873 --> 00:04:02,175
Ready, now.

78
00:04:03,977 --> 00:04:05,245
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

79
00:04:05,845 --> 00:04:08,114
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>

80
00:04:08,248 --> 00:04:09,749
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

81
00:04:09,882 --> 00:04:13,119
<i>Her solo weapons are her license</i>

82
00:04:13,186 --> 00:04:14,287
<i>and the skills that she has earned.</i>

83
00:04:14,354 --> 00:04:16,089
Don't push. Just hang in there.

84
00:04:16,556 --> 00:04:17,590
Coming through!

85
00:04:18,791 --> 00:04:20,960
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

86
00:04:21,661 --> 00:04:22,629
<i>Also known as</i>

87
00:04:23,196 --> 00:04:24,931
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

88
00:04:53,326 --> 00:04:55,361
My goodness.

89
00:04:56,062 --> 00:04:57,997
What should we do?

90
00:05:03,569 --> 00:05:05,605
Was he caught in the affair?

91
00:05:06,105 --> 00:05:07,073
Look.

92
00:05:07,407 --> 00:05:08,274
This is...

93
00:05:08,341 --> 00:05:10,143
Even though she's in the second trimester,

94
00:05:10,476 --> 00:05:12,612
she's showing signs of mitral stenosis.

95
00:05:12,745 --> 00:05:15,581
As the blood circulation
is boosted during pregnancy,

96
00:05:16,716 --> 00:05:19,585
there is a risk of rapid heart failure.

97
00:05:20,253 --> 00:05:23,589
There's a chance of failing to
save both the mother and the baby.

98
00:05:25,758 --> 00:05:27,593
It'd be best to wait until the delivery.

99
00:05:27,760 --> 00:05:29,696
However, it can be

100
00:05:29,896 --> 00:05:30,997
extremely dangerous

101
00:05:31,064 --> 00:05:32,732
for the mother's body.

102
00:05:35,134 --> 00:05:35,968
Ouch.

103
00:05:38,871 --> 00:05:39,739
What should we do?

104
00:05:39,872 --> 00:05:42,508
We have no choice but to
operate as quickly as possible.

105
00:05:43,076 --> 00:05:45,144
Let me do this heart operation.

106
00:05:45,211 --> 00:05:47,547
What do you think
you're saying, Daimon?

107
00:05:47,613 --> 00:05:50,216
No one else other than you
would think of administering...

108
00:05:50,283 --> 00:05:52,618
anaesthetics to a pregnant woman
and opening her up.

109
00:05:53,019 --> 00:05:54,053
What about the baby, then?

110
00:05:54,420 --> 00:05:57,523
I will not do a heart operation
that carries twice the risk.

111
00:05:58,391 --> 00:06:00,960
That's why I said that I'll do it.

112
00:06:01,160 --> 00:06:02,195
Daimon, wait. Wait!

113
00:06:02,261 --> 00:06:03,663
Daimon!

114
00:06:03,730 --> 00:06:06,265
- Chief!
- What is it?

115
00:06:07,033 --> 00:06:11,337
Her husband, Wang Chao,
is here at the hospital.

116
00:06:13,239 --> 00:06:15,675
What are we going to do?

117
00:06:19,679 --> 00:06:20,546
At last,

118
00:06:21,914 --> 00:06:24,283
the chief and her husband
will have a fiery showdown?

119
00:06:24,684 --> 00:06:26,119
- Stop it.
- Goodness.

120
00:06:26,652 --> 00:06:27,787
- What should I do?
- What?

121
00:06:27,854 --> 00:06:29,355
- What should I do?
- What's wrong?

122
00:06:29,422 --> 00:06:30,923
Calm down. Hara...

123
00:06:30,990 --> 00:06:36,396
What should I do? What should I do?

124
00:06:37,163 --> 00:06:37,997
Wait.

125
00:06:41,367 --> 00:06:42,235
Where is she?

126
00:06:42,602 --> 00:06:43,770
Where is his wife?

127
00:06:44,137 --> 00:06:46,606
Her examination is complete

128
00:06:46,672 --> 00:06:50,076
and she is resting in the deluxe suite.

129
00:06:51,778 --> 00:06:55,081
Mr. Wang, about the results
of your wife's examination...

130
00:06:56,816 --> 00:06:57,717
Excuse me.

131
00:06:58,317 --> 00:06:59,152
Who are you?

132
00:06:59,252 --> 00:07:00,820
I am a surgeon, Michiko Daimon.

133
00:07:01,287 --> 00:07:03,289
There is something urgent
I need to talk to you.

134
00:07:03,990 --> 00:07:07,026
Your life will be in danger
if you don't get a heart surgery.

135
00:07:08,361 --> 00:07:09,562
Please let me preform your surgery.

136
00:07:10,997 --> 00:07:13,399
Is that Dr. Saionji's diagnosis?

137
00:07:13,533 --> 00:07:15,902
No, but it's an emergency.

138
00:07:20,106 --> 00:07:23,075
With mitral stenosis,
my heart becomes dysfunctional,

139
00:07:23,142 --> 00:07:24,677
making it hard to give birth.

140
00:07:25,678 --> 00:07:27,513
That's what they told me
at the hospital in China as well.

141
00:07:27,814 --> 00:07:31,017
But, you do not need
to treat my heart condition.

142
00:07:31,083 --> 00:07:31,951
Why not?

143
00:07:32,852 --> 00:07:34,554
Do you know who my husband is?

144
00:07:36,355 --> 00:07:39,292
Some kind of filthy rich
man in China or something?

145
00:07:40,393 --> 00:07:43,996
Please put the baby's life... before mine.

146
00:07:46,098 --> 00:07:46,933
What?

147
00:07:48,568 --> 00:07:49,769
I need you...

148
00:07:49,836 --> 00:07:51,871
to put the safe birth of my child...

149
00:07:53,206 --> 00:07:56,843
above my wife's life.

150
00:07:57,844 --> 00:07:59,045
Please put the safe birth

151
00:07:59,412 --> 00:08:02,482
of his child above the mother's life.

152
00:08:05,117 --> 00:08:06,118
Are you saying...

153
00:08:07,086 --> 00:08:11,190
it doesn't matter to you
what happens to your wife?

154
00:08:19,131 --> 00:08:20,333
THE UNBORN BABY

155
00:08:21,100 --> 00:08:25,004
IS AN IMPORTANT HEIR TO THE WANG GROUP

156
00:08:25,304 --> 00:08:26,272
The unborn baby...

157
00:08:27,173 --> 00:08:29,575
is an important heir
to the Wang group.

158
00:08:31,344 --> 00:08:32,211
Well, but...

159
00:08:32,345 --> 00:08:34,113
- Do you have a problem with that?
- Do you have a problem with that?

160
00:08:36,082 --> 00:08:36,949
No.

161
00:08:41,687 --> 00:08:43,022
Excuse me.

162
00:08:43,956 --> 00:08:47,059
I knew it. Dr. Daimon, let's go.

163
00:08:47,760 --> 00:08:50,730
So you mean you want to save your baby

164
00:08:50,897 --> 00:08:53,699
only if the father of the baby
turns out to be your husband, right?

165
00:08:53,833 --> 00:08:54,901
Dr. Daimon!

166
00:08:54,967 --> 00:08:56,002
What do you mean?

167
00:08:56,068 --> 00:08:58,404
- What if it is a child born of adultery?
- Stop it!

168
00:08:58,471 --> 00:08:59,305
Adultery?

169
00:08:59,438 --> 00:09:00,940
I saw you...

170
00:09:01,374 --> 00:09:03,976
with Dr. Saionji at a shrine
wishing for a safe delivery.

171
00:09:06,412 --> 00:09:11,050
So, if the baby isn't the heir
to the Wang group,

172
00:09:11,117 --> 00:09:12,051
it's another story.

173
00:09:12,184 --> 00:09:14,353
- Dr. Daimon, that's enough!
- Be quiet!

174
00:09:14,420 --> 00:09:17,790
Just hurry up and get the
operation, and be healthy.

175
00:09:18,190 --> 00:09:19,959
- Who on earth are you?
- What?

176
00:09:20,192 --> 00:09:23,396
I thought you were a strange
female doctor, but you're too weird.

177
00:09:32,638 --> 00:09:36,208
Oh my. This is ridiculous.

178
00:09:37,209 --> 00:09:39,412
I haven't laughed this much
for a long time.

179
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:42,882
The reason I went there
with Dr. Saionji...

180
00:09:43,182 --> 00:09:45,685
is because my husband
is Christian.

181
00:09:45,952 --> 00:09:47,553
So I asked Dr. Saionji instead.

182
00:09:47,687 --> 00:09:48,654
Oh, is that so?

183
00:09:50,222 --> 00:09:52,425
Is that really true?

184
00:09:55,461 --> 00:09:57,263
I swear to this charm that

185
00:09:57,330 --> 00:09:58,397
I am not cheating on my husband.

186
00:10:00,232 --> 00:10:02,835
We apologise.

187
00:10:03,235 --> 00:10:08,975
Dr. Saionji is so kind...
that you could misunderstand him.

188
00:10:09,041 --> 00:10:10,309
But it's because I am rich.

189
00:10:10,509 --> 00:10:11,377
What do you mean?

190
00:10:11,444 --> 00:10:13,579
Everyone bows down
in front of my husband's wealth.

191
00:10:14,146 --> 00:10:17,216
The life of the child who will
inherit the immense fortune...

192
00:10:18,284 --> 00:10:20,453
is much more valuable
than that of mine.

193
00:10:22,188 --> 00:10:24,857
Huh? Do you really think so?

194
00:10:27,193 --> 00:10:33,165
I didn't come here for you to fix
my heart condition. But to give birth.

195
00:10:35,368 --> 00:10:37,703
I have nothing more to talk about.

196
00:10:42,074 --> 00:10:46,245
The Wang group is about to
open its own hospitals in China.

197
00:10:46,612 --> 00:10:48,547
It's a gigantic firm.

198
00:10:48,614 --> 00:10:49,949
That's incredible.

199
00:10:50,016 --> 00:10:53,185
If the operation is a success,
I'm sure the reward will be huge.

200
00:10:53,252 --> 00:10:55,221
Michiko, do your best.

201
00:10:55,287 --> 00:10:57,556
I can't. She already said no.

202
00:10:57,690 --> 00:10:58,591
What?

203
00:10:59,158 --> 00:11:01,427
I don't really get rich people.

204
00:11:01,661 --> 00:11:05,665
She said the child's life
is more important than her own.

205
00:11:05,998 --> 00:11:09,301
That isn't because she is rich,

206
00:11:09,435 --> 00:11:10,636
it is because she is a mother.

207
00:11:11,570 --> 00:11:15,007
If it is for my child,
my own life doesn't matter.

208
00:11:15,775 --> 00:11:17,677
All mothers would think the same.

209
00:11:17,877 --> 00:11:20,212
- Really?
- Yes.

210
00:11:21,714 --> 00:11:22,815
By the way,

211
00:11:22,882 --> 00:11:25,718
Mai will come home from England
during her winter break, right?

212
00:11:26,385 --> 00:11:28,487
You must be proud of her.

213
00:11:28,754 --> 00:11:30,923
I wonder what kind of
ballerina she will become.

214
00:11:33,392 --> 00:11:34,593
It's your turn, Jonouchi.

215
00:11:35,094 --> 00:11:36,162
What's wrong?

216
00:11:36,228 --> 00:11:39,432
Nothing, my lower back is stiff.

217
00:11:39,799 --> 00:11:40,900
I have shoulder pain.

218
00:11:40,966 --> 00:11:43,102
- We are getting old.
- You're right.

219
00:11:43,436 --> 00:11:45,638
Teaching her ballet costs a lot.

220
00:11:45,771 --> 00:11:47,406
I have to do a lot of surgeries
and make money.

221
00:11:47,473 --> 00:11:49,542
That's right. Mothers are strong!

222
00:11:52,311 --> 00:11:53,145
Oh, I won!

223
00:11:53,379 --> 00:11:55,748
I've got the full pieces.

224
00:11:57,216 --> 00:11:59,452
- What?
- You're too good.

225
00:12:00,152 --> 00:12:04,857
Director Hiruma will now lead
his rounds around the hospital.

226
00:12:04,924 --> 00:12:10,796
I wonder how Ms. Wang
likes her deluxe suite.

227
00:12:12,264 --> 00:12:14,867
Well, how about treating them...
as a model celebrity birth case...

228
00:12:14,934 --> 00:12:18,404
and holding a press conference?

229
00:12:18,504 --> 00:12:19,472
That's a good idea.

230
00:12:19,872 --> 00:12:23,442
Well, honestly...

231
00:12:23,509 --> 00:12:27,046
What is it?
Why do you look so grim, Saionji?

232
00:12:27,113 --> 00:12:28,214
We've undertaken

233
00:12:28,848 --> 00:12:30,082
the physical examination...

234
00:12:31,450 --> 00:12:34,320
and found mitral stenosis.

235
00:12:34,453 --> 00:12:35,554
What?

236
00:12:35,621 --> 00:12:39,091
However, the husband has
made his desire clear that

237
00:12:39,158 --> 00:12:42,061
the baby's life should be prioritised.

238
00:12:42,695 --> 00:12:43,596
I see.

239
00:12:44,597 --> 00:12:50,102
How about trying your best
to save both mother and child.

240
00:12:50,803 --> 00:12:52,505
- What do you think?
- I think it's difficult.

241
00:12:52,571 --> 00:12:53,706
- Is that so?
- Yes.

242
00:12:54,140 --> 00:12:56,609
- Then...
- What should we do?

243
00:12:56,809 --> 00:12:59,145
If that's the case,

244
00:12:59,612 --> 00:13:05,151
then I suppose we must
follow her husband's desires.

245
00:13:05,217 --> 00:13:10,489
We must do our best to make sure
a healthy heir is born without problems.

246
00:13:11,924 --> 00:13:13,159
I think that's the best.

247
00:13:13,626 --> 00:13:14,660
Okay.

248
00:13:14,794 --> 00:13:15,828
Yes sir.

249
00:13:17,897 --> 00:13:19,331
What is it, Assistant Director?

250
00:13:19,765 --> 00:13:21,400
Why are you saying
such dumb things?

251
00:13:22,401 --> 00:13:24,837
Foremost, you should be
treating the pregnant woman.

252
00:13:25,371 --> 00:13:26,972
The pregnant woman must come first.

253
00:13:27,573 --> 00:13:30,075
Women are not
child-bearing machines!

254
00:13:30,876 --> 00:13:35,381
There are two different kinds...
of happiness women can have.

255
00:13:35,748 --> 00:13:37,983
You incredibly trampled
on other women...

256
00:13:38,250 --> 00:13:40,286
and obtained the current position.

257
00:13:40,686 --> 00:13:42,721
However, all that

258
00:13:43,889 --> 00:13:47,993
is waiting for you after retirement
may be lonely death.

259
00:13:49,795 --> 00:13:52,431
Before that happens,

260
00:13:52,631 --> 00:13:55,334
why don't you apologise
to the women you trampled on...

261
00:13:55,768 --> 00:13:58,270
and become happy?

262
00:13:58,337 --> 00:14:00,206
Thank you, Ms. Kubo.

263
00:14:00,272 --> 00:14:02,608
It was my pleasure working
with you for a long time.

264
00:14:03,375 --> 00:14:07,112
I won't quit until you drop dead.

265
00:14:08,547 --> 00:14:10,683
Stop talking so loud!

266
00:14:14,220 --> 00:14:15,321
Oh, watch out.

267
00:14:15,387 --> 00:14:18,123
Hey! Don't get in our way like that!

268
00:14:18,324 --> 00:14:19,859
- I will.
- Huh?

269
00:14:21,627 --> 00:14:22,595
Excuse me.

270
00:14:22,862 --> 00:14:24,029
You're here again?

271
00:14:24,096 --> 00:14:25,231
Yes, I am.

272
00:14:25,464 --> 00:14:27,967
I think I am the best fit
for this surgery.

273
00:14:28,901 --> 00:14:31,403
PTMC using a balloon catheter.

274
00:14:32,705 --> 00:14:35,908
We will insert a balloon catheter
into a vein in your leg...

275
00:14:35,975 --> 00:14:37,676
and thread it to your heart.

276
00:14:43,282 --> 00:14:45,651
We will then expand
the tip of the balloon...

277
00:14:45,718 --> 00:14:47,620
inside of the stenosed part of
the vein to increase blood flow.

278
00:14:47,686 --> 00:14:48,954
With this procedure,

279
00:14:49,188 --> 00:14:53,525
the risks to both you and your baby

280
00:14:53,592 --> 00:14:55,294
will be very low,

281
00:14:55,361 --> 00:14:58,197
so it will be possible for you
to continue your pregnancy...

282
00:14:58,330 --> 00:15:00,699
and even give birth
by caesarian section.

283
00:15:00,766 --> 00:15:02,101
Oh my.

284
00:15:04,536 --> 00:15:05,905
Such loud volume...

285
00:15:06,205 --> 00:15:08,407
can make the baby startled.

286
00:15:09,241 --> 00:15:10,276
The doctor here

287
00:15:10,476 --> 00:15:12,444
keeps intruding and is quite annoying.

288
00:15:16,048 --> 00:15:18,817
Japanese doctors are paid too little.

289
00:15:19,551 --> 00:15:21,820
I'm sure she just wants a tip.

290
00:15:25,424 --> 00:15:28,127
Please take this.
I will give you more later.

291
00:15:28,460 --> 00:15:30,696
Thanks in advance...

292
00:15:30,763 --> 00:15:31,797
I don't want any tips!

293
00:15:33,599 --> 00:15:37,169
You're not trying to persuade
your wife, so I'm doing it for you!

294
00:15:37,603 --> 00:15:39,271
If we don't hurry the operation,

295
00:15:39,338 --> 00:15:41,273
your wife will die!

296
00:15:42,741 --> 00:15:43,676
Hey! Translate it.

297
00:15:45,778 --> 00:15:46,612
WHAT DID SHE SAY?

298
00:15:47,479 --> 00:15:48,347
Excuse me.

299
00:15:49,615 --> 00:15:52,151
- Dr. Daimon!
- We are so sorry again.

300
00:15:52,217 --> 00:15:55,421
We will take every measure to make
sure this doesn't happen again.

301
00:15:55,487 --> 00:15:56,789
WHAT EXACTLY IS GOING ON?

302
00:15:56,855 --> 00:15:59,124
I'm sorry. Let's get out, Dr. Daimon.

303
00:15:59,191 --> 00:16:01,060
- What? I'm not done talking.
- Hurry.

304
00:16:02,127 --> 00:16:03,395
It hurts!

305
00:16:03,462 --> 00:16:05,064
What is it this time?

306
00:16:05,130 --> 00:16:06,966
- Ouch!
- What is it?

307
00:16:07,967 --> 00:16:09,668
What is going on?

308
00:16:10,202 --> 00:16:12,271
- Mr. Wang is offended.
- Huh?

309
00:16:12,504 --> 00:16:15,007
If Dr. Daimon doesn't
leave her alone...

310
00:16:15,274 --> 00:16:17,409
and keep pushing to
have a heart surgery,

311
00:16:18,010 --> 00:16:19,812
- she'll move to another hospital.
- What?

312
00:16:19,912 --> 00:16:21,246
You must be kidding.

313
00:16:21,380 --> 00:16:22,948
Do you know how big the loss it is

314
00:16:23,182 --> 00:16:25,317
to lose a pregnant celebrity?

315
00:16:26,085 --> 00:16:28,687
You don't need to come here.

316
00:16:28,754 --> 00:16:31,390
You need to be more stern.
You're on suspension!

317
00:16:32,992 --> 00:16:36,996
You're missing great opportunities
to become a happy woman.

318
00:16:37,162 --> 00:16:41,667
You're heading straight
to a lonely death.

319
00:16:41,867 --> 00:16:43,335
Before it's too late,

320
00:16:43,469 --> 00:16:44,737
how about...

321
00:16:44,803 --> 00:16:47,406
- getting married?
- Huh?

322
00:16:48,307 --> 00:16:51,210
Like I said...
Well, nothing. Forget it.

323
00:16:51,610 --> 00:16:55,314
You're on suspension now,
so go home.

324
00:16:58,884 --> 00:17:00,319
How boring.

325
00:17:02,621 --> 00:17:04,990
I don't care about getting married.
I just want to eat pork cutlet.

326
00:17:06,558 --> 00:17:07,893
Oh, Jonouchi...

327
00:17:14,500 --> 00:17:16,135
Adultery with the
pregnant woman's husband?

328
00:17:20,539 --> 00:17:22,441
Michiko, calm down.

329
00:17:22,641 --> 00:17:24,943
I'm sure she decided to
give birth in Japan...

330
00:17:25,010 --> 00:17:27,946
because she knew she'd die

331
00:17:28,347 --> 00:17:30,649
if she did it in China.

332
00:17:30,983 --> 00:17:32,351
Right, Ben Casey?

333
00:17:35,421 --> 00:17:37,122
I ran into someone unexpectedly.

334
00:17:37,189 --> 00:17:38,023
A guest?

335
00:17:38,157 --> 00:17:39,525
- Please come in.
- Ms. Kubo.

336
00:17:39,591 --> 00:17:42,327
Hello. Excuse me.

337
00:17:42,394 --> 00:17:45,697
Are you here to play mah-jong again?
It's already late!

338
00:17:46,865 --> 00:17:47,933
Isn't she silly?

339
00:17:48,167 --> 00:17:51,703
She's on the suspension,
but all she thinks about is surgery.

340
00:17:51,937 --> 00:17:53,639
Women are all the same!

341
00:17:53,839 --> 00:17:55,107
We are like-minded.

342
00:17:55,908 --> 00:17:56,842
Dr. Daimon,

343
00:17:57,076 --> 00:18:00,813
I brought your favourite dish.

344
00:18:03,382 --> 00:18:04,883
- Gyoza?
- Yes.

345
00:18:05,617 --> 00:18:06,752
Here you are.

346
00:18:09,988 --> 00:18:10,889
It's delicious.

347
00:18:10,956 --> 00:18:13,292
So, what brought you here?

348
00:18:13,926 --> 00:18:17,062
I want Ms. Wang to get the heart
surgery as soon as possible.

349
00:18:17,796 --> 00:18:22,935
However, neither the husband
nor wife would agree with it.

350
00:18:23,001 --> 00:18:24,303
But I'm sure Michiko

351
00:18:24,369 --> 00:18:26,572
will end up with suspension again.

352
00:18:26,705 --> 00:18:28,173
Why don't you let the patient...

353
00:18:28,674 --> 00:18:31,844
get a thorough check-up once again?

354
00:18:32,010 --> 00:18:34,313
Tell her this time
it's a test related to the baby.

355
00:18:35,114 --> 00:18:36,615
That's a good idea.

356
00:18:37,716 --> 00:18:41,787
I'm sure they are ready...
to do anything if it's for the baby.

357
00:18:42,488 --> 00:18:44,690
- Please eat more.
- Thank you.

358
00:18:46,625 --> 00:18:49,895
By the way, what were you
talking about in the car earlier?

359
00:18:50,129 --> 00:18:51,096
Huh?

360
00:18:51,163 --> 00:18:55,968
I saw you. You got out of
the limousine with Wang Chan.

361
00:18:59,071 --> 00:19:01,440
He asked me about anaesthesia...

362
00:19:01,673 --> 00:19:04,009
in case she delivers her baby
by caesarian section.

363
00:19:06,178 --> 00:19:08,347
No melon today?

364
00:19:08,580 --> 00:19:10,616
Unfortunately, I didn't
buy any today.

365
00:19:10,749 --> 00:19:12,417
SONOGRAPHY ROOM 12

366
00:19:33,205 --> 00:19:34,373
How is your condition?

367
00:19:35,340 --> 00:19:36,241
Let me see...

368
00:19:37,209 --> 00:19:38,477
- Clean her up.
- Okay.

369
00:19:39,311 --> 00:19:41,813
- Ouch.
- What is wrong with you?

370
00:19:43,916 --> 00:19:47,019
There is a large tumour
on the baby's chest.

371
00:19:47,886 --> 00:19:48,720
What?

372
00:19:51,223 --> 00:19:52,724
My goodness.

373
00:19:53,692 --> 00:19:56,895
It is significantly hindering
the growth of the baby's lungs,

374
00:19:57,129 --> 00:19:58,330
putting pressure on the heart.

375
00:19:58,664 --> 00:20:01,300
If we don't remove the tumour,
the baby's heart will stop.

376
00:20:02,367 --> 00:20:04,603
Considering the mother's
heart condition,

377
00:20:05,704 --> 00:20:10,142
the only option is to abort the fetus...
and save the mother's life.

378
00:20:30,395 --> 00:20:32,931
There are things one cannot
do anything about.

379
00:20:34,333 --> 00:20:35,701
Do you think so?

380
00:20:42,941 --> 00:20:47,913
We can perform the operation
quickly and save your wife.

381
00:20:49,948 --> 00:20:53,552
Or you can just wait for the baby
to die in her body.

382
00:20:55,220 --> 00:20:57,289
There are only two options.

383
00:21:10,836 --> 00:21:11,837
This can't be right.

384
00:21:18,543 --> 00:21:19,478
Miss,

385
00:21:21,113 --> 00:21:23,782
I know it is hard,
but please make a decision.

386
00:21:25,951 --> 00:21:26,785
No.

387
00:21:31,657 --> 00:21:33,992
I don't care what happens to me.

388
00:21:36,561 --> 00:21:42,200
Please, no matter what happens...
save my baby.

389
00:21:43,802 --> 00:21:44,703
Doctor...

390
00:21:47,039 --> 00:21:48,774
Doctor, please.

391
00:21:54,713 --> 00:21:58,050
The patient this time is
the wife of a billionaire,

392
00:21:58,116 --> 00:21:59,651
Mr. Chao Wang.
She's 30 years old.

393
00:21:59,818 --> 00:22:01,953
She has been diagnosed
with mitral stenosis.

394
00:22:02,087 --> 00:22:04,589
She is 21 weeks into pregnancy.

395
00:22:04,956 --> 00:22:07,092
And a large tumour has been found
on the fetus and...

396
00:22:07,192 --> 00:22:09,294
is putting pressure
on the heart and the lungs.

397
00:22:10,429 --> 00:22:13,231
Unavoidably,
we will perform an abortion...

398
00:22:13,298 --> 00:22:17,436
then surgically repair the mitral
valve and continue with treatment.

399
00:22:17,502 --> 00:22:20,138
Please leave it to me!
It's internal medicine's turn.

400
00:22:20,739 --> 00:22:24,443
Before the mitral valve surgery,
we plan to treat her...

401
00:22:24,509 --> 00:22:26,211
with medicines such as diuretic
and beta blockers.

402
00:22:26,278 --> 00:22:28,947
Furthermore, in preparation
for future pregnancies,

403
00:22:29,014 --> 00:22:31,717
freezing her embryos is
also being considered.

404
00:22:31,883 --> 00:22:32,718
I have an objection.

405
00:22:35,554 --> 00:22:38,457
Hey, why is the part-timer
on suspension still here?

406
00:22:38,523 --> 00:22:42,394
It seems as though Ms. Kubo
newly contracted with her.

407
00:22:43,328 --> 00:22:45,163
Now she's sticking
by Ms. Kubo's side.

408
00:22:45,230 --> 00:22:48,266
She really has no honour.

409
00:22:48,333 --> 00:22:52,571
Dr. Daimon, please continue.
What is your objection?

410
00:22:53,505 --> 00:22:55,374
I will not allow an abortion.

411
00:22:57,376 --> 00:23:01,179
Are you going to say you can treat
both the mother and the baby?

412
00:23:01,246 --> 00:23:02,948
- Correct!
- Oh, I got it.

413
00:23:03,248 --> 00:23:04,082
Are you mocking me?

414
00:23:04,216 --> 00:23:07,819
If we operate on both
of them simultaneously,

415
00:23:08,120 --> 00:23:10,355
we can save them both.

416
00:23:10,489 --> 00:23:12,791
A simultaneous mother
and fetus surgery?

417
00:23:16,728 --> 00:23:18,530
First, we will perform a PTMC

418
00:23:18,797 --> 00:23:20,499
with the balloon and widen the valve.

419
00:23:20,699 --> 00:23:21,933
Then, operate on the fetus.

420
00:23:22,267 --> 00:23:25,370
We will take the upper half of the fetus
out of the uterus, and remove the tumour.

421
00:23:25,637 --> 00:23:27,539
Do you really think you can do
such an impossible surgery?

422
00:23:27,606 --> 00:23:28,807
I can do it.

423
00:23:31,877 --> 00:23:32,811
Then, you must perform

424
00:23:32,878 --> 00:23:38,116
both operations very quickly
in order to save both of them.

425
00:23:38,417 --> 00:23:39,751
You can't do it alone.

426
00:23:40,085 --> 00:23:43,488
Who on earth would ever want
to assist such reckless surgery?

427
00:23:43,755 --> 00:23:44,990
Is there anyone?

428
00:23:50,362 --> 00:23:51,663
Are you all cowards?

429
00:23:56,101 --> 00:23:56,968
There he is.

430
00:23:57,035 --> 00:23:58,203
Dr. Kaji, are you
really going to do it?

431
00:23:58,270 --> 00:24:00,539
- My back its itchy.
- Okay.

432
00:24:03,308 --> 00:24:06,077
I want to operate on one of them.

433
00:24:06,178 --> 00:24:07,879
Would you approve it?

434
00:24:09,681 --> 00:24:11,183
- Sure.
- Kitano.

435
00:24:17,422 --> 00:24:19,624
Challenge is progress.

436
00:24:21,660 --> 00:24:25,630
I don't really like that
weird English, but let's do this.

437
00:24:26,465 --> 00:24:30,202
Wait, Daimon! Daimon!
You must do as Mr. Wang wants!

438
00:24:30,569 --> 00:24:32,571
Daimon!

439
00:24:35,707 --> 00:24:37,375
What is the success rate?

440
00:24:37,909 --> 00:24:39,778
It is an extremely
dangerous surgery.

441
00:24:39,845 --> 00:24:43,048
We'll do with all our might,
but the risk is 50 percent.

442
00:24:43,114 --> 00:24:44,516
I never fail.

443
00:24:45,150 --> 00:24:46,818
Your Chinese pronunciation is good.

444
00:24:51,456 --> 00:24:52,524
I'll give up after all.

445
00:24:54,359 --> 00:24:55,427
I'm giving up on the child.

446
00:24:56,228 --> 00:24:58,096
He will...

447
00:24:58,864 --> 00:25:00,098
just give up on the baby.

448
00:25:02,634 --> 00:25:05,103
I don't care how dangerous
the surgery is.

449
00:25:06,872 --> 00:25:07,706
I...

450
00:25:11,343 --> 00:25:13,144
trust this doctor.

451
00:25:24,155 --> 00:25:27,325
Dr. Daimon, please.

452
00:25:32,063 --> 00:25:35,600
Please save... my baby.

453
00:25:44,109 --> 00:25:47,145
I never fail.

454
00:26:11,269 --> 00:26:15,273
During the operation tomorrow,
keep your eyes on the baby's vitals.

455
00:26:18,577 --> 00:26:19,578
Dr. Jonouchi?

456
00:26:21,012 --> 00:26:23,114
I will. I know what I should do.

457
00:26:28,520 --> 00:26:31,122
Jonouchi hasn't been around lately.

458
00:26:31,990 --> 00:26:34,492
I wonder if that rumour
could be true by chance.

459
00:26:34,793 --> 00:26:35,794
What rumour?

460
00:26:36,561 --> 00:26:39,130
It's been said that the Wang group...

461
00:26:39,431 --> 00:26:40,966
is scouting the best doctors
from Toutei University hospital...

462
00:26:41,032 --> 00:26:43,768
for their own hospitals in China
with a promise of high payrolls.

463
00:26:47,038 --> 00:26:51,643
They already suggested that Dr. Kitano
work at their hospital in Shanghai.

464
00:26:52,544 --> 00:26:53,912
I'm happy to hear that.

465
00:26:54,112 --> 00:26:55,680
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

466
00:26:58,617 --> 00:27:00,685
So that's why he suddenly
volunteered for the operation.

467
00:27:00,852 --> 00:27:02,887
I thought it was strange.

468
00:27:03,355 --> 00:27:06,858
He'd do anything
to appeal to Mr. Wang.

469
00:27:06,925 --> 00:27:08,860
Then, Jonouchi also
received the same offer?

470
00:27:09,127 --> 00:27:10,729
I think so.

471
00:27:11,162 --> 00:27:13,531
I heard from a source that...

472
00:27:13,598 --> 00:27:15,133
she was scouted at the same time
as Dr. Kitano.

473
00:27:19,571 --> 00:27:21,940
She did say she wanted money.

474
00:27:22,741 --> 00:27:24,009
Maybe she'll quit and go there.

475
00:27:24,142 --> 00:27:28,313
This is bad. If we compete
with Chinese money power,

476
00:27:28,380 --> 00:27:31,650
small firms like ours
will completely be crushed.

477
00:27:42,460 --> 00:27:43,595
What is it?

478
00:27:44,329 --> 00:27:46,631
Is it true that you were
scouted by the Wang group?

479
00:27:50,368 --> 00:27:52,570
Oh, you already knew it?

480
00:27:53,938 --> 00:27:56,207
You must never fail today.

481
00:27:56,675 --> 00:27:59,477
I have to show the new hospital
just how good I am.

482
00:28:05,383 --> 00:28:06,317
Excuse me.

483
00:28:07,485 --> 00:28:08,920
This is a wonderful room.

484
00:28:08,987 --> 00:28:09,854
Please have a seat.

485
00:28:23,401 --> 00:28:24,536
Let's get it started.

486
00:28:27,472 --> 00:28:29,407
We have one doctor missing.

487
00:28:30,208 --> 00:28:31,643
I don't hear any weird English.

488
00:28:33,611 --> 00:28:34,913
Hey, everybody.

489
00:28:35,380 --> 00:28:36,781
Sorry for the wait.

490
00:28:37,282 --> 00:28:39,651
He did it on purpose
to make his presence known.

491
00:28:39,718 --> 00:28:40,685
What a scumbag.

492
00:28:47,258 --> 00:28:48,093
We need to hurry.

493
00:28:48,259 --> 00:28:53,531
We will now begin the simultaneous
operations on the mother and the fetus.

494
00:28:53,698 --> 00:28:56,634
It will be co-performed
by myself and Dr. Daimon.

495
00:28:57,168 --> 00:28:58,737
First, we will start
with the PTMC,

496
00:28:58,803 --> 00:29:01,372
using a balloon catheter
to widen the mitral valve.

497
00:29:01,439 --> 00:29:02,507
- Scalpel.
- Here you are.

498
00:29:07,145 --> 00:29:08,847
18 gauge syringe.

499
00:29:12,684 --> 00:29:14,652
Is it really okay
to put a scalpel...

500
00:29:14,986 --> 00:29:16,287
inside of a fetus?

501
00:29:16,354 --> 00:29:17,188
Be quiet.

502
00:29:20,425 --> 00:29:21,593
- Guide catheter.
- Here you are.

503
00:29:40,879 --> 00:29:42,247
- Sir.
- Yes?

504
00:29:43,948 --> 00:29:44,883
I am watching.

505
00:29:47,152 --> 00:29:49,687
By any chance,

506
00:29:51,356 --> 00:29:55,426
if we cannot save both of them,

507
00:29:56,461 --> 00:29:57,829
what will happen?

508
00:30:01,666 --> 00:30:04,803
Daimon, you must be extra cautious.

509
00:30:05,904 --> 00:30:08,673
You know what will happen
if you fail.

510
00:30:10,742 --> 00:30:13,077
I never fail.

511
00:30:18,016 --> 00:30:19,584
It reached the left ventricle.

512
00:30:19,818 --> 00:30:21,352
Let's inflate the balloon.

513
00:30:21,519 --> 00:30:22,887
Hold it steadily.

514
00:30:22,954 --> 00:30:24,022
All right.

515
00:30:28,026 --> 00:30:28,893
Inflation.

516
00:30:32,297 --> 00:30:35,834
Now, I will fixate the balloon.

517
00:30:40,104 --> 00:30:41,172
I'm going to pull slightly.

518
00:30:44,142 --> 00:30:45,610
Inflating again.

519
00:30:50,281 --> 00:30:52,550
SURGERY HOUR

520
00:30:53,318 --> 00:30:55,420
The operation on the mother is
complete. What are her vitals?

521
00:30:55,553 --> 00:30:58,656
Vitals are 115 and 82.
Heart rate is 85.

522
00:30:58,723 --> 00:30:59,757
What is the heart rate of the fetus?

523
00:31:06,331 --> 00:31:07,198
138.

524
00:31:07,465 --> 00:31:09,067
Then, I'll remove the tumour
from the fetus.

525
00:31:09,133 --> 00:31:11,135
- Scalpel.
- Here.

526
00:31:21,312 --> 00:31:22,547
- Monopolar.
- Here you are.

527
00:31:28,019 --> 00:31:29,954
She's so fast.

528
00:31:31,990 --> 00:31:33,925
Finally, she has begun
the baby's surgery.

529
00:31:41,966 --> 00:31:43,434
The uterus incision is complete.

530
00:31:44,102 --> 00:31:45,703
- Give me tools for the fetus.
- Okay.

531
00:31:55,313 --> 00:31:56,281
WHAT IS SHE DOING?

532
00:31:56,881 --> 00:31:57,882
What is she doing?

533
00:31:58,082 --> 00:32:02,220
The size of the only
21-weeks-old fetus is...

534
00:32:02,387 --> 00:32:03,688
is only 25 centimetres.

535
00:32:04,022 --> 00:32:06,391
So, they must use very small tools.

536
00:32:06,457 --> 00:32:09,594
Its heart is as small as a cherry.

537
00:32:10,461 --> 00:32:13,364
The tumour is the size of a tangerine.

538
00:32:18,436 --> 00:32:20,405
Please also prepare for closing.

539
00:32:20,538 --> 00:32:22,073
- Lower my magnifiers.
- Excuse me.

540
00:32:22,507 --> 00:32:23,374
Excuse me.

541
00:32:23,441 --> 00:32:27,011
If the fetus is exposed from
the uterus too much,

542
00:32:27,512 --> 00:32:30,748
the risk of temperature decline,
infection, fluid loss...

543
00:32:30,815 --> 00:32:32,517
and early birth will increase.

544
00:32:32,583 --> 00:32:33,418
Furthermore,

545
00:32:34,552 --> 00:32:40,525
the risk of death by shock of the mother
due to excessive bleeding increases.

546
00:32:47,298 --> 00:32:50,301
I will now take the fetus
out of the uterus.

547
00:33:07,085 --> 00:33:09,087
Dr. Kaji, hold the fetus.

548
00:33:09,420 --> 00:33:10,254
Got it.

549
00:33:13,891 --> 00:33:15,259
I will now make an incision
in the fetus' chest.

550
00:33:15,460 --> 00:33:16,394
- Scalpel.
- Here.

551
00:33:16,627 --> 00:33:19,030
I'll take on the operation
on the fetus.

552
00:33:21,199 --> 00:33:23,201
The rib cage is still brittle,
so be careful.

553
00:33:23,267 --> 00:33:27,305
If you damage the organs
that were pressed by the tumour,

554
00:33:27,372 --> 00:33:28,439
the baby will die.

555
00:33:35,813 --> 00:33:38,383
Will you really let her
perform the most important part?

556
00:33:38,449 --> 00:33:41,252
Women have smaller hands,
so she'll do better.

557
00:33:44,022 --> 00:33:45,556
Okay, I'll do it.

558
00:34:10,481 --> 00:34:11,883
Tumour removal is complete.

559
00:34:18,589 --> 00:34:20,625
Let's put the fetus
back into the uterus.

560
00:34:21,359 --> 00:34:22,460
- Bipolar.
- Here.

561
00:34:25,696 --> 00:34:28,066
The baby's heart rate is decreasing.

562
00:34:29,567 --> 00:34:30,468
Dr. Daimon.

563
00:34:30,535 --> 00:34:31,369
What are the vitals?

564
00:34:34,105 --> 00:34:36,207
Dr. Jonouchi,
what are the vitals?

565
00:34:37,175 --> 00:34:38,509
Its heart rate is dropping.

566
00:34:38,910 --> 00:34:41,112
It's 85... 72.

567
00:34:41,312 --> 00:34:42,647
The uterus is haemorrhaging.

568
00:34:42,713 --> 00:34:44,182
Her blood pressure is dropping.

569
00:34:46,818 --> 00:34:48,553
Prepare for a blood transfusion.

570
00:34:48,686 --> 00:34:49,520
Okay.

571
00:34:52,590 --> 00:34:53,424
Daimon,

572
00:34:53,791 --> 00:34:56,561
give up the fetus
and concentrate on the mother!

573
00:34:56,994 --> 00:34:58,763
Dr. Daimon, stay level-headed!

574
00:35:07,038 --> 00:35:08,172
Why is this happening?

575
00:35:11,075 --> 00:35:12,210
It's okay.

576
00:35:12,810 --> 00:35:15,113
Dr. Daimon never fails.

577
00:35:19,951 --> 00:35:20,785
Why?

578
00:35:22,086 --> 00:35:23,087
Calm down.

579
00:35:24,889 --> 00:35:28,526
I'll support you,
so directly massage the heart.

580
00:35:31,095 --> 00:35:33,331
- Open the uterus.
- Got it.

581
00:35:57,722 --> 00:35:58,723
No way.

582
00:36:01,526 --> 00:36:02,493
Will they fail?

583
00:36:42,233 --> 00:36:45,069
The heart is pumping.

584
00:36:47,939 --> 00:36:49,607
The heart is pumping again.

585
00:36:50,741 --> 00:36:52,443
She saved the baby.

586
00:36:55,279 --> 00:36:58,149
It is a miracle.

587
00:37:00,451 --> 00:37:03,120
All right.
Close the baby's chest up.

588
00:37:05,056 --> 00:37:07,225
Give the mother a blood transfusion.

589
00:37:07,358 --> 00:37:08,192
Got it.

590
00:37:10,261 --> 00:37:11,963
I can't believe it.

591
00:37:20,104 --> 00:37:21,305
Thank goodness.

592
00:37:24,375 --> 00:37:27,712
How could she pull it off?
Michiko Daimon.

593
00:37:31,916 --> 00:37:34,018
The surgery is complete.
The baby's vitals?

594
00:37:35,119 --> 00:37:36,854
Heart rate is 130.

595
00:37:36,921 --> 00:37:38,055
What about the mother?

596
00:37:38,456 --> 00:37:44,195
Blood pressure is less than 115...
over 82. Heart rate is 85.

597
00:37:52,870 --> 00:37:54,538
Your baby did great as well.

598
00:37:56,674 --> 00:37:57,508
Dr. Daimon.

599
00:38:00,611 --> 00:38:01,679
It was very impressive.

600
00:38:05,316 --> 00:38:06,517
It was terrific.

601
00:38:06,651 --> 00:38:09,654
- It was terrific.
- It was!

602
00:38:10,788 --> 00:38:11,689
Thank you so much.

603
00:38:11,889 --> 00:38:13,324
Thank you so much.

604
00:38:22,099 --> 00:38:24,201
TOUTEI UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

605
00:38:32,610 --> 00:38:33,644
Excuse me.

606
00:38:34,478 --> 00:38:36,213
Dr. Kaji. Ms. Kubo.

607
00:38:38,049 --> 00:38:40,117
She always goes home
right after surgery.

608
00:38:40,184 --> 00:38:41,886
What's gotten into her today?

609
00:38:42,453 --> 00:38:44,822
Maybe she's hoping to be scouted
by the Wang group...

610
00:38:44,889 --> 00:38:45,923
and wants some brownie points.

611
00:38:46,023 --> 00:38:47,024
- Dr. Kaji.
- I'm joking.

612
00:38:47,091 --> 00:38:48,292
I know that.

613
00:39:08,779 --> 00:39:11,615
The conditions of both of you
are stable now.

614
00:39:15,152 --> 00:39:16,420
Thank you very much.

615
00:39:19,890 --> 00:39:23,761
It was an extremely risky surgery.

616
00:39:34,338 --> 00:39:36,607
One, two, three.

617
00:39:36,674 --> 00:39:37,541
Cheese.

618
00:39:38,509 --> 00:39:40,177
It's great.

619
00:39:43,013 --> 00:39:45,649
That female doctor is truly skilled.

620
00:39:46,417 --> 00:39:49,587
She is a freelance doctor
who will go anywhere if she's paid.

621
00:39:49,720 --> 00:39:51,255
I will take her to your hospital.

622
00:40:00,564 --> 00:40:02,700
Michiko is late. Let's eat first.

623
00:40:03,167 --> 00:40:05,736
Here you are. Eat up.

624
00:40:05,803 --> 00:40:06,704
Thank you.

625
00:40:07,471 --> 00:40:10,074
I'm always on the side
of single mothers.

626
00:40:10,508 --> 00:40:12,510
I'll help you as much as I can,

627
00:40:13,144 --> 00:40:15,112
so please don't go to Shanghai.

628
00:40:21,419 --> 00:40:22,319
Mr. Akira...

629
00:40:23,154 --> 00:40:24,855
- I'm home.
- Welcome home.

630
00:40:25,055 --> 00:40:26,390
You're late.

631
00:40:26,524 --> 00:40:28,259
- Aren't you hungry?
- I'm hungry.

632
00:40:36,801 --> 00:40:37,835
You're hopeless.

633
00:40:38,969 --> 00:40:42,640
Are you going to fight
all of a sudden? Stop that.

634
00:40:42,706 --> 00:40:43,908
It's okay, Mr. Akira.

635
00:40:44,175 --> 00:40:46,811
I made a mistake
during the operation.

636
00:40:46,944 --> 00:40:50,514
You made a mistake?
I can't believe it.

637
00:40:50,648 --> 00:40:54,051
She told me never to take my eyes
off of the baby's vitals.

638
00:40:56,921 --> 00:40:57,788
I'm sorry.

639
00:40:58,789 --> 00:41:02,193
I performed too many operations
recently, so I was exhausted.

640
00:41:02,993 --> 00:41:07,331
You're a human, too. It happens.

641
00:41:10,034 --> 00:41:11,635
Don't attend the operations.
I'm in charge of anymore.

642
00:41:14,472 --> 00:41:17,708
It'd be better to let her
take a rest for a while.

643
00:41:17,975 --> 00:41:19,677
If an anaesthetist makes
such mistake,

644
00:41:20,110 --> 00:41:21,145
patients can die.

645
00:41:21,512 --> 00:41:25,149
Michiko, stop it.
Or she might go to Shanghai.

646
00:41:25,583 --> 00:41:27,852
If she does,
you will be the one in trouble.

647
00:41:30,120 --> 00:41:32,022
Daimon never fails,

648
00:41:33,257 --> 00:41:35,159
so you can't forgive
even one mistake.

649
00:41:35,292 --> 00:41:36,393
I can't.

650
00:41:40,364 --> 00:41:41,232
I see.

651
00:41:44,034 --> 00:41:44,935
Okay.

652
00:41:48,305 --> 00:41:53,277
If you take it this far, I can't work
with you any longer, either.

653
00:41:56,380 --> 00:41:58,816
Now I can move to Shanghai
with a light heart.

654
00:41:59,383 --> 00:42:01,352
Both of you, stop it.

655
00:42:01,418 --> 00:42:02,586
Dr. Jonouchi.

656
00:42:03,888 --> 00:42:05,756
Isn't there something else
you are hiding from us?

657
00:42:17,001 --> 00:42:19,937
Mr. Akira, although it wasn't long,

658
00:42:20,437 --> 00:42:22,606
thank you for everything.

659
00:42:25,042 --> 00:42:28,078
Michiko, follow her and apologise.

660
00:42:31,715 --> 00:42:34,218
I made this hot pot for you two,
and it's gone to waste.

661
00:42:37,521 --> 00:42:38,589
Michiko.

662
00:42:50,200 --> 00:42:51,101
Michiko!

663
00:43:07,117 --> 00:43:09,219
Hello? Mai?

664
00:43:11,288 --> 00:43:14,224
Well, why don't we
spend Christmas...

665
00:43:14,959 --> 00:43:17,895
in Shanghai instead of Tokyo?

666
00:43:19,863 --> 00:43:23,167
Right. You can't meet with
Mr. Akira and Dr. Daimon this time,

667
00:43:23,601 --> 00:43:26,737
but Christmas Eve in Shanghai
is wonderful as well.

668
00:43:29,306 --> 00:43:31,141
We can stay in a nice hotel,

669
00:43:31,709 --> 00:43:35,212
set up a tree together... and eat cake.

670
00:43:40,618 --> 00:43:41,452
Yes.

671
00:43:43,253 --> 00:43:47,358
Well, I will call you again later, Mai.

672
00:43:57,234 --> 00:43:59,870
Dr. Jonouchi, are you okay?

673
00:44:00,671 --> 00:44:01,605
Dr. Daimon,

674
00:44:02,906 --> 00:44:05,576
I'm fine.

675
00:44:09,980 --> 00:44:11,115
Hey!

676
00:44:14,518 --> 00:44:17,121
Help me! Call an ambulance!

677
00:44:17,187 --> 00:44:19,490
No! Don't tell anyone.

678
00:44:20,424 --> 00:44:22,960
Why didn't you treat it
before it's gone this bad?

679
00:44:23,427 --> 00:44:24,895
Why didn't you tell me about it?

680
00:44:28,132 --> 00:44:31,001
Gosh. You knew about it?

681
00:44:32,569 --> 00:44:34,405
Of course, you did, Dr. Daimon.

682
00:44:40,811 --> 00:44:45,315
I'm sorry, Mai.

683
00:44:46,183 --> 00:44:47,484
Hang in there,

684
00:44:47,551 --> 00:44:48,452
Dr. Jonouchi.

685
00:44:49,520 --> 00:44:51,055
Dr. Jonouchi!

686
00:44:51,188 --> 00:44:54,058
Someone, call an ambulance!

687
00:44:54,825 --> 00:44:56,093
Call an ambulance!

688
00:44:56,894 --> 00:44:58,162
Help me!

689
00:44:59,630 --> 00:45:01,532
THE FINAL EPISODE

690
00:45:01,865 --> 00:45:03,067
Let me operate.

691
00:45:03,500 --> 00:45:05,536
I need you to stay alive.

692
00:45:05,803 --> 00:45:07,271
I wanted to keep working longer.

693
00:45:07,337 --> 00:45:09,573
With this, you can keep working.

694
00:45:09,707 --> 00:45:11,842
Blood pressure is falling.
She doesn't stop bleeding!
